nL43:     * 【25†serde_json ^1.0.150 dev】\nL44:   * Versions\nL45:   *     * 【26†0.9.0-rc.1 (2026-10-11)】\nL46:     * 【27†0.8.0 (2026-09-23)】\nL47:     * 【28†0.7.0 (2026-09-04)】\nL48:     * 【29†0.7.0-rc.1 (2026-08-19)】\nL49:     * 【30†0.6.3 (2026-07-30)】\nL50:     * 【31†0.6.2 (2026-07-20)】\nL51:     * 【32†0.6.1 (2026-06-13)】\nL52:     * 【33†0.6.0 (2026-06-11)】\nL53: \nL54:   * Owners\nL55:   * Sumcheck protocol implementation for multilinear polynomial verification.\nL56: # The Sumcheck Protocol\nL57: \nL58: The sumcheck protocol verifies a claimed sum of the form:\nL59: \nL60:     `sum_{x in {0,1}^l} g(x) = t\nL61:     `\nL62: \nL63: Without it, the verifier would need to evaluate `g` at all `2^l` hypercube points. The protocol reduces this to a single evaluation at a random point, using `l` rounds.\nL64: \nL65: In each round, the prover sends a low-degree univariate polynomial:\nL66: \nL67:     `h_i(X) = sum_{x_{i+1}, ..., x_l in {0,1}} g(r_1, ..., r_{i-1}, X, x_{i+1}, ..., x_l)\nL68:     `\nL69: The verifier checks `h_i(0) + h_i(1) == claimed_sum`. Then samples a random challenge `r_i` and updates the claim to `h_i(r_i)`.\nL70: \nL71: After `l` rounds, the verifier holds `(r_1, ..., r_l)` and queries `g` directly.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndeep-prove/zkml/README.md at master · Lagrange-Labs/deep-prove · GitHub (https://github.com/Lagrange-Labs/deep-prove/blob/master/zkml/README.md)\nciteturn10view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/Lagrange-Labs/deep-prove/blob/master/zkml/README.md\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 441\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3:   * Products\nL4: \nL5:     *       * 【1†GitHub Repository hosting, code review, and collaboration】\nL6:       * 【2†Copilot AI coding agent for tasks, projects and automated work】\nL7: \nL8:     * Build & Ship\nL9:       * 【3†Actions CI/CD and automation】\nL10:   